Pipeline done, all five stages plus tree search.

**Final CV: MCRMSE 0.444076** (honest — blend weights re-fit leave-one-outer-fold-out; the same blend reads 0.428772 when weights are fit in-sample). `competitions/afsis-soil-properties/submission.csv` written, 727 rows, columns and PIDN order verified identical to `sample_submission.csv`.

How it got there. EDA found the load-bearing fact: the 15 spatial covariates take only 580 distinct values across 1157 rows, because 565 sites each contribute a Topsoil/Subsoil pair — so validation is a GroupKFold over those site signatures, nested with an inner GroupKFold(4) that picks each target's ridge alpha using outer-train rows only. Features were five spectral preprocessing variants with the CO2 band dropped. The linear protocol produced a 16-config solo pool (best: SVR-RBF on SG-d1, 0.471939) and one blend at 0.433219, which satisfied the tree-search entry condition. Tree search then ran 80 nodes in 74 seconds and its champion, the mandatory explore-burst kitchen-sink blend, beat the linear best at evaluation 17.

The finding worth keeping is a negative one. My first tree-search run re-seeded only 4 of the 16 linear-pool solos, and its blend scored 0.449717 — *worse* than the linear blend it was meant to beat. Re-seeding the whole pool as first-generation lineages (free, via cached-OOF reuse) with no other change moved the champion to 0.428772. I initially blamed the weight-search method and was wrong: at 64 members greedy 0.428772, Dirichlet 0.428899, bagged greedy 0.430371 — the method is a second-order knob, member diversity was the whole gap. Both the run-1 tree and that result are kept (`experiments_tree_v3_run1_diluted_blend.json`, experiment #6), and the corrected insight is in `knowledge/experience.md` along with the hypothesis-was-wrong note.

Caveats stated plainly in STATUS.md: everything is OOF-only, since this competition closed in 2014 and nothing was submitted to Kaggle. The champion's 0.000127 margin over the second-best blend is noise; the ~0.0043 gap to the 16-member blends and ~0.040 to the best solo are not. The measured greedy-weight optimism, +0.015304, lands inside the +0.0146–0.0186 band the experience library predicted. The search stopped on the hard budget cap with the burst still improving, so more budget would likely still buy a little.
